.TH APPNEST 1 "" "appnest" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appnest \- manage, integrate, and launch AppImages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appnest
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appnest
is a graphical manager for AppImage files. It imports AppImages into a library,
creates application menu entries and icons for them, launches and stops them,
and can calculate their SHA-256 hashes.
.PP
If one or more AppImage files are given on the command line, AppNest opens its
window and offers to add or run each of them. Only one instance runs at a time;
files passed to a second invocation are handled by the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
AppNest accepts the standard GTK and GApplication options. It does not provide a command-line interface for managing AppImages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the available options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Show all options, including those of GTK.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-gapplication
Show the GApplication options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appnest/
Managed AppImages, extracted AppDirs, icons and the application database
(default: \fI~/.local/share/appnest/\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/appnest/config.toml
User settings (default: \fI~/.config/appnest/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/
Desktop entries generated for integrated AppImages (named appnest-<id>.desktop).
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/appnest/launch-<id>.log
Standard error output of the most recent launch of an application.
